From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 09:05:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sunxi: Set the DMA mask from the descriptor address
 shift

Controllers with idma_des_shift address 34 bits through the shifted
IDMAC fields, but keep the default 32-bit DMA mask. On boards with DRAM
above 4 GiB every request then bounces through swiotlb.

Set the mask to 32 + idma_des_shift bits before the descriptors are
allocated, and fall back to bounce buffers with a warning if it is
refused.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards (8 and 6 GiB); reading 2
GiB from the SD card leaves the swiotlb high-water mark at 0, and no DMA
mask warning is logged.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
index d24fc97ea5b1..6ae07a72b31b 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
@@ -1387,6 +1387,16 @@ static int sunxi_mmc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * The IDMAC takes buffer and descriptor addresses shifted right by
+	 * idma_des_shift, so it reaches that many bits beyond 32.
+	 */
+	ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(&pdev->dev,
+					DMA_BIT_MASK(32 + host->cfg->idma_des_shift));
+	if (ret)
+		dev_warn(&pdev->dev, "cannot use %u-bit DMA addresses\n",
+			 32 + host->cfg->idma_des_shift);
+
 	host->sg_cpu = dma_alloc_coherent(&pdev->dev, PAGE_SIZE,
 					  &host->sg_dma, GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!host->sg_cpu) {
